格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Your coding agents remember what you decided — and what you changed. Plain-Markdown memory in Obsidian, shared by Claude Code, Codex and Cursor over MCP. Every answer cites its page; when the vault does not know, it says so. Imports your past sessions on install.","id":"gh:1341648244","install_available":true,"language":"Python","name":"KRouter","slug":"398894496-arch/KRouter","topics":["agent-memory","ai-agents","chinese","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","codex","cursor","deepseek","dsh-plugin","knowledge-base","mcp","mcp-server","obsidian","persistent-memory","pkm","second-brain","sqlite-fts5","windows","zero-config"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Your coding agents remember what you decided — and what you changed. Plain-Markdown memory in Obsidi"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"an, shared by Claude Code, Codex and Cursor over MCP. Every answer cites its page; when the vault do"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"es not know, it says so. Imports your past sessions on install."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# KRouter"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Your AI remembers what you decided — and what you changed your mind about.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Works with the AI you already use, and one is enough. Your memory is a folder of plain Markdown page"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"s you can open,\nread and edit, in Obsidian or any editor. Ask \"what did we decide about the cover ti"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"tle?\" and\nthe answer comes with the page it came from. A correction replaces the old answer instead "},{"id":"p4s4","text":"of competing with it. When\nthe memory does not know, your AI is told so, rather than handed somethin"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"g close. Code, writing, video, study or\nwork: anything you decide and later change."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"[](https://github.com/398894496-arch/KRouter/actions/workflows/ci.yml) [](https://github.com/3988944"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"96-arch/KRouter/releases/latest) [](LICENSE) · 中文：`README.zh.md`"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Tests run on Linux, macOS and Windows on every push. The one-line install downloads the latest relea"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"se (a tag, never\n`main`) and checks its SHA-256 before running anything; each release also carries a"},{"id":"p6s3","text":" GitHub build-provenance\nattestation (`gh attestation verify <package> --repo 398894496-arch/KRouter"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"`). What you ask never leaves your machine."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Measured, not claimed"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**On other people's benchmarks**, scored from their authors' own labels, no model judge:\n- **LongMem"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"Eval** (ICLR 2025; 500 questions, each over about 50 chat sessions): for 439 of 470 answerable quest"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ions an\nanswer session is among the pages KRouter cites; for 70 of 72 questions whose fact changed l"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ater, it cites the\nnewest one.\n- **LoCoMo** (ACL 2024; 1,986 questions over 10 long conversations): "},{"id":"p8s5","text":"the first page cited holds the evidence for 991\nof 1,540 answerable questions, and one of the top th"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"d holds the evidence for 991\nof 1,540 answerable questions, and one of the top three does for 1,204."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"These count whether the right page was found, not whether a model then answered correctly, so they d"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"o not line up with\nthe answer-accuracy percentages other projects publish. Plain BM25 finds about as"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" many pages (447 / 470, 968 / 1,540)."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**Where it is weak:** a question about a near neighbour of something the memory does mention still g"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ets an answer. It\nrefuses 3 of 30 LongMemEval questions that have no answer, and 37 of 446 LoCoMo tr"},{"id":"p10s3","text":" It\nrefuses 3 of 30 LongMemEval questions that have no answer, and 37 of 446 LoCoMo trick questions."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**On our own 200 held-out questions** (English and Chinese, never tuned on, written by Claude Opus i"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"n separate\nsessions): KRouter cites a wrong page 26% of the time; claude-mem 64%, basic-memory 78%. "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"Of 80 questions the memory\ncannot answer, it refuses 47; the other two refuse none. Of 60 questions "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"about a decision that was later changed, it\ngets 50 right; they get 34 and 16. Part of that gap is b"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"y construction: plain full-text search given KRouter's two\nrules is level with it. What KRouter adds"},{"id":"p11s6","text":" is having those rules on by default, plus receipts and a memory you can edit.\nEvery number and its "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"les on by default, plus receipts and a memory you can edit.\nEvery number and its method · rerun them"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Windows (PowerShell): `irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/398894496-arch/KRouter/main/scripts/boo"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"tstrap.ps1 | iex` · Claude Code plugin: `/plugin install krouter --marketplace 398894496-arch/KRoute"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"r` (Claude Code 2.1.275 or later; from a shell, `claude plugin install krouter --marketplace 3988944"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"96-arch/KRouter` needs 2.1.292). Third-party marketplaces do not auto-update: run `claude plugin upd"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"ate krouter@krouter`, or turn it on in `/plugin` → Marketplaces → krouter → Enable auto-update."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Rather look first? Nothing below changes your machine until the last line:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Python 3 is the only requirement. The installer makes a memory folder (or uses yours with `--vault`,"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" overwriting\nnothing), connects Claude Code and Codex to it through MCP when they are installed, and"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" stops there: lookup only, no\nquestions, nothing leaves the machine. Another app? See Works with. Wh"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"en you want it to start\nremembering, run the line it prints last (`bootstrap.py --ask`), which asks "},{"id":"p17s5","text":" to start\nremembering, run the line it prints last (`bootstrap.py --ask`), which asks two questions."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Works with"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| App | How it connects | Status |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Claude Code | plugin, or MCP (the installer registers it) | tested |\n| Codex | MCP (the installer "},{"id":"p20s2","text":"registers it) | tested |\n| Cursor | rule and skill (the installer adds them) | tested |\n| DeepSeek H"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"arness | plugin (`dsh plugin --profile web add github:398894496-arch/KRouter`) | tested |\n| Any app "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"that runs a local MCP server: Claude Desktop, VS Code, Windsurf, Zed, Gemini CLI, … | add the server"},{"id":"p20s5","text":" below to the app's MCP settings | should work, not yet tested by us: tell us |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Use the full path to your home folder (on Windows, `C:\\\\Users\\\\you\\\\.agents\\\\…` and often `python` i"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"nstead of\n`python3`). After the one-line install the server finds your memory by itself. It is stand"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ard-library Python over\nstdio with two read-only tools, `krouter_ask` and `krouter_status`; a plain "},{"id":"p22s4","text":"MCP client gets through `initialize`,\n`tools/list`, a cited answer and `recall: none` from it."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## What leaves your machine"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Queries never do: lookup is a local SQLite full-text index, about 110 ms. Session import is local. T"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ext goes to a model only for the steps you said yes to: distilling sessions and nightly upkeep. It g"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"oes to the CLI or API key you already use, and `--dry-run` shows the size first. Keys and pages mark"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ed secret are never sent or quoted. For the nightly writer, the API-key lane runs nothing on\nyour ma"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"chine; CLI lanes differ in what they can read, and the install says which one you are choosing. Deta"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"ffer in what they can read, and the install says which one you are choosing. Details:\n`SECURITY.md`."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"**Backups.** `backup.py init --dir <a folder that syncs elsewhere>` turns on a nightly encrypted arc"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"hive of the whole\nvault, history included, opened again each night before it counts. Point it at iCl"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"oud Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, a\nNetdisk sync folder or a USB disk (or two of them); KRouter talks to"},{"id":"p25s4","text":" no cloud. Why this and not syncing or pushing the\nvault: `DETAILS.md` → Backing up your vault."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

